{
  "name": "monkfish",
  "_about": "SCULPTED (2026-11-21, tools/creaturegen/rework/fish/monkfish.py): a monkfish (angler), 1.0 m -- a HUGE BROAD FLAT HEAD that is most of the fish, the body tapering behind it to a small square tail; an ENORMOUS MOUTH slotted across the whole front, the pale lower jaw jutting, both jaws lined with long inward-raking TEETH (`horn`s); the first dorsal spine a fishing rod (the ILLICIUM) arching forward over the mouth with a fleshy LURE on its tip, two more free spines behind it; small eyes on top of the head under bony brows; a FRINGE of skin flaps round the jaw and along the head's rim; big fleshy arm-like pectorals, small pelvics under the throat, the soft dorsal and the anal far back; MOTTLED brown above (the coat pattern `mottle`), pale below. Each fin is one membrane sheet. A slow SWIMMER that lies on the bottom (the fish's plumbing).",
